 "findings": [
  "Pooled across every state and territory (federal elections 2001, 2004, 2007, 2010, 2013, 2016, 2019, 2022, 2025): where Labor governed the state, federal Labor's swing there was -0.4 points relative to the national swing compared with states under the Coalition (permutation p = 0.58): no sign that voters punish their state government at federal elections.",
  "Within each state (when the state government changed party between federal elections): -0.6 points (p = 0.50), from 19 changes of government.",
  "Victoria (state government 2001 ALP, 2004 ALP, 2007 ALP, 2010 ALP, 2013 COAL, 2016 ALP, 2019 ALP, 2022 ALP, 2025 ALP); its deviations from the national swing were 2001 +0.5, 2004 -1.4, 2007 -0.2, 2010 +3.6, 2013 -1.5, 2016 -1.5, 2019 +2.5, 2022 -2.0, 2025 -1.6 points.",
  "Same party at both levels: -0.03 points per unit (positive would mean a state government of the federal government's party helps it federally).",
  "69 state-elections."
 ]
